WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.108 --> 00:00:02.677
- [Narrator] Coastal at one moment,

00:00:02.677 --> 00:00:04.846
isolated island at another,

00:00:04.846 --> 00:00:09.013
Mont Saint-Michel is incredibly
stunning no matter the tide.

00:00:12.264 --> 00:00:15.217
In between two powerful tides
from Normandy and Brittany

00:00:15.217 --> 00:00:18.861
stands the gothic-styled
Benedictine Abbey named after

00:00:18.861 --> 00:00:23.508
and dedicated to the
archangel Saint Michael.

00:00:23.508 --> 00:00:25.669
Mont Saint-Michel wasn't always an island.

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:28.294
In prehistoric times,
it stood on dry land.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:32.319
However, as sea levels rose,
erosion reshaped the coast.

00:00:32.319 --> 00:00:36.900
Even today, it only sits
600 meters from land.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.593
Although it has less than
50 full-time residents,

00:00:39.593 --> 00:00:43.630
it is visited by more than
three million people each year.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.967
The climb to see the abbey isn't easy.

00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:47.800
It's around 900 steps.

00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:52.462
More than just a church on a rock,

00:00:52.462 --> 00:00:55.053
Mont Saint-Michel is a
medieval time capsule

00:00:55.053 --> 00:00:57.690
and was one of the first
monuments to be classed

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.523
as a UNESCO World Heritage
Site back in 1979.

